<section class="section">
      <div class="container inner-page-content">
        <p>Professor Jerry RV is committed to providing clear information, responsible service, and fair, objective
          observations. The following principles describe how we intend to conduct our business.</p>
        <h2>Honesty and transparency</h2>
        <p>We communicate findings and recommendations truthfully, distinguish observed facts from opinions, and explain
          material limitations or uncertainties. We do not knowingly misrepresent an RV's condition or the scope of work
          performed.</p>
        <h2>Independence and objectivity</h2>
        <p>RV inspection findings should be based on the inspection performed, not on pressure from buyers, sellers,
          dealers, or advertisers. We disclose material conflicts of interest and decline or appropriately manage
          engagements where independence cannot be maintained.</p>
        <h2>Competence and scope</h2>
        <p>We accept work consistent with our training, qualifications, tools, and applicable requirements. When a
          problem calls for specialized expertise or licensed work outside our scope, we explain that limitation and
          recommend an appropriate qualified professional.</p>
        <h2>Safety first</h2>
        <p>We place the safety of owners, occupants, and technicians ahead of convenience. We do not encourage unsafe
          shortcuts, and we identify safety concerns when they are discovered within the agreed scope of work.</p>
        <h2>Education and respect</h2>
        <p>We explain RV systems in understandable terms, encourage questions, and treat customers with patience and
          respect. Our purpose is to help owners make informed decisions, not to overwhelm them with jargon or
          unnecessary services.</p>
        <h2>Clear expectations and fair dealing</h2>
        <p>We strive to describe the scope, limitations, fees, and deliverables of an engagement before work begins. We
          communicate significant changes and avoid recommending work solely to generate additional revenue.</p>
        <h2>Confidentiality</h2>
        <p>We handle customer information, photographs, and reports with care and share them only as authorized or
          otherwise permitted or required. Specific confidentiality obligations may also be established in the service
          agreement.</p>
        <h2>Professional standards</h2>
        <p>Where applicable, inspections and technical services will be conducted in accordance with the standards,
          agreements, and legal requirements governing the particular engagement. This page expresses our business
          commitments; it does not replace any applicable professional code, inspection standard, or signed agreement.
        </p>
        <h2>Questions or concerns</h2>
        <p>If you have a concern about our conduct or a service we provided, please contact <a
            href="mailto:info@ProfessorJerryRV.com">info@ProfessorJerryRV.com</a> so we can review it.</p>
      </div>
    </section>
